IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VI: "Offences and Punishment" (ss 135 to 137), "Social Insurance Number"
-- (ss 138 to 141) and "Reports" (ss 142 and 143). Piece ei4. Layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- Conventions as in ei4-part-vi-review.l4. In addition:
--   * A maximum or a minimum is a figure the text states; "not more than double X" is a cap, so the rule returns the greatest amount
--     the court may add, never an amount the court must impose.
--   * "A fine of not less than $200 and not more than $5,000 plus ..." is carried as the least fine, the greatest fine before the
--     addition, and the greatest addition; a sentence is checked against them by a separate rule.
--   * Whether an offence "knowingly" or "knows" was committed is the person's state of mind and is taken as a fact in the record.
-- Hohfeld, for these sections: the state's power to prosecute and punish is the person's liability; a penalty already imposed under
-- s 38, 39 or 65.1 is the person's immunity from prosecution for the same offence (s 135(2)); the duty to have a Social Insurance
-- Number and to report a change of name is owed to the Commission, whose claim is the correlative.

§ `Part VI -- Offences and Punishment`

§§ `s 135(1) Offence`

-- One record for the conduct alleged. Each field is one paragraph of subsection (1) (the paragraph is in the comment).
-- src:2012 | 135 (1) Every person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:2013 | (a) in relation to a claim for benefits, makes a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading;
-- src:2014 | (b) being required under this Act or the regulations to provide information, provides information or makes a representation the person knows to be false or misleading;
-- src:2015 | (b.1) knowingly fails to declare to the Commission all or some of their earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which they claimed benefits;
-- src:2016 | (c) makes a claim or declaration that the person knows is false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts;
-- src:2017 | (d) being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiates or attempts to negotiate it for benefits to which the person is not entitled;
-- src:2018 | (e) knowingly fails to return a special warrant, or the amount or any excess amounts, as required by section 44;
-- src:2019 | (f) imports or exports a document issued by the Commission, or has it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission; or
-- src:2020 | (g) participates in, assents to or acquiesces in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (f).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(1) (src:2012-2020)
DECLARE `ei4 Conduct alleged under section 135(1)` HAS
    `in relation to a claim for benefits, made a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `being required under this Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `knowingly failed to declare to the Commission all or some of their earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which they claimed benefits` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b.1)
    `made a claim or declaration that the person knows is false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiated or attempted to negotiate it for benefits to which the person is not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `knowingly failed to return a special warrant, or the amount or any excess amounts, as required by section 44` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e); out of range: section 44 (piece ei2)
    `imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)
    `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (g)

-- src:2012 | 135 (1) Every person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:2013 | (a) in relation to a claim for benefits, makes a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading;
-- src:2014 | (b) being required under this Act or the regulations to provide information, provides information or makes a representation the person knows to be false or misleading;
-- src:2015 | (b.1) knowingly fails to declare to the Commission all or some of their earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which they claimed benefits;
-- src:2016 | (c) makes a claim or declaration that the person knows is false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts;
-- src:2017 | (d) being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiates or attempts to negotiate it for benefits to which the person is not entitled;
-- src:2018 | (e) knowingly fails to return a special warrant, or the amount or any excess amounts, as required by section 44;
-- src:2019 | (f) imports or exports a document issued by the Commission, or has it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission; or
-- src:2020 | (g) participates in, assents to or acquiesces in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (f).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(1) (src:2012-2020)
GIVEN conduct IS A `ei4 Conduct alleged under section 135(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 135(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` IF
       conduct's `in relation to a claim for benefits, made a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading`
    OR conduct's `being required under this Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading`
    OR conduct's `knowingly failed to declare to the Commission all or some of their earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which they claimed benefits`
    OR conduct's `made a claim or declaration that the person knows is false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts`
    OR conduct's `being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiated or attempted to negotiate it for benefits to which the person is not entitled`
    OR conduct's `knowingly failed to return a special warrant, or the amount or any excess amounts, as required by section 44`
    OR conduct's `imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission`
    OR conduct's `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (f)`

§§ `s 135(2) Saving`

-- src:2022 | (2) No prosecution for an offence under this section shall be instituted if a penalty for that offence has been imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(2) (src:2022)
GIVEN `a penalty for that offence has been imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: sections 38 and 39 (piece ei2), section 65.1 (piece ei2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 135(2) a prosecution for the offence may be instituted` IF
    NOT (`a penalty for that offence has been imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1`)

§§ `s 135(3) Punishment`

-- The figures the text states.
-- src:2025 | (a) a fine of not less than $200 and not more than $5,000 plus,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(3)(a) (src:2025)
`s 135(3)(a) the least fine` MEANS 200

-- src:2025 | (a) a fine of not less than $200 and not more than $5,000 plus,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(3)(a) (src:2025)
`s 135(3)(a) the greatest fine before any addition` MEANS 5000

-- src:2028 | (b) both the fine and imprisonment for a term of not more than six months.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(3)(b) (src:2028)
`s 135(3)(b) the longest term of imprisonment, in months` MEANS 6

-- (i): "an amount of not more than double the total of" the two amounts; a cap on the addition.
-- src:2026 | (i) in a case mentioned in paragraph (1)(b.1), an amount of not more than double the total of the amount by which the person’s benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3) and the amount of the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period mentioned in that paragraph if the benefits had not been reduced or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits, or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(3)(a)(i) (src:2026)
GIVEN `the amount by which the person's benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 19 (piece ei1)
      `the amount of the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period if the benefits had not been reduced or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 135(3)(a)(i) the greatest addition in a case under paragraph (1)(b.1)` IS
    2 TIMES (`the amount by which the person's benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)` PLUS `the amount of the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period if the benefits had not been reduced or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits`)

-- src:2027 | (ii) in any other appropriate case, an amount of not more than double the amount of any benefits that may have been paid as a result of committing the offence; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(3)(a)(ii) (src:2027)
GIVEN `the amount of any benefits that may have been paid as a result of committing the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 135(3)(a)(ii) the greatest addition in any other appropriate case` IS
    2 TIMES `the amount of any benefits that may have been paid as a result of committing the offence`

-- The greatest fine. "In any other appropriate case" is the court's judgment, so it is an input; when the case is neither a paragraph
-- (1)(b.1) case nor an appropriate case, nothing is added to the $5,000.
-- src:2024 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under this section is liable to
-- src:2025 | (a) a fine of not less than $200 and not more than $5,000 plus,
-- src:2026 | (i) in a case mentioned in paragraph (1)(b.1), an amount of not more than double the total of the amount by which the person’s benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3) and the amount of the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period mentioned in that paragraph if the benefits had not been reduced or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits, or
-- src:2027 | (ii) in any other appropriate case, an amount of not more than double the amount of any benefits that may have been paid as a result of committing the offence; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(3)(a) (src:2024-2027)
GIVEN `the offence is a case mentioned in paragraph (1)(b.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an appropriate case for an addition under subparagraph (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount by which the person's benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period if the benefits had not been reduced or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of any benefits that may have been paid as a result of committing the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 135(3)(a) the greatest fine` IS
    `s 135(3)(a) the greatest fine before any addition` PLUS
        (BRANCH IF `the offence is a case mentioned in paragraph (1)(b.1)`
                THEN `s 135(3)(a)(i) the greatest addition in a case under paragraph (1)(b.1)`
                         `the amount by which the person's benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)`
                         `the amount of the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period if the benefits had not been reduced or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits`
                IF `the case is an appropriate case for an addition under subparagraph (ii)`
                THEN `s 135(3)(a)(ii) the greatest addition in any other appropriate case` `the amount of any benefits that may have been paid as a result of committing the offence`
                OTHERWISE 0)

-- A sentence of a fine alone, or of the fine and imprisonment, is within the limits when the fine lies between the least and the
-- greatest fine and any imprisonment is not more than six months. Imprisonment comes only "with" the fine (paragraph (b)).
-- src:2024 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under this section is liable to
-- src:2025 | (a) a fine of not less than $200 and not more than $5,000 plus,
-- src:2026 | (i) in a case mentioned in paragraph (1)(b.1), an amount of not more than double the total of the amount by which the person’s benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3) and the amount of the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period mentioned in that paragraph if the benefits had not been reduced or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits, or
-- src:2027 | (ii) in any other appropriate case, an amount of not more than double the amount of any benefits that may have been paid as a result of committing the offence; or
-- src:2028 | (b) both the fine and imprisonment for a term of not more than six months.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 135(3) (src:2024-2028)
GIVEN `the fine` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the greatest fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 135(3) the punishment is within the limits` IF
        `the fine` AT LEAST `s 135(3)(a) the least fine`
    AND `the fine` AT MOST `the greatest fine`
    AND `the term of imprisonment, in months` AT MOST `s 135(3)(b) the longest term of imprisonment, in months`

§§ `s 136 Contravention of Act or regulations`

-- src:2030 | 136 (1) Every person who contravenes this Act or the regulations is guilty of an offence.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 136(1) (src:2030)
GIVEN `contravenes this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 136(1) the person is guilty of an offence` IF
    `contravenes this Act or the regulations`

-- src:2032 | (2) Every person who delays or obstructs a person authorized by the Commission in exercising their powers or performing their duties under this Act or the regulations is guilty of an offence.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 136(2) (src:2032)
GIVEN `delays a person authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `obstructs a person authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person delayed or obstructed is exercising their powers or performing their duties under this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 136(2) the person is guilty of an offence` IF
        (`delays a person authorized by the Commission` OR `obstructs a person authorized by the Commission`)
    AND `the person delayed or obstructed is exercising their powers or performing their duties under this Act or the regulations`

§§ `s 137 General penalty for offences`

-- src:2034 | 137 Every person who is guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is provided is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $100 and not more than $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than six months, or to both.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 137 (src:2034)
`s 137 the least fine` MEANS 100

-- src:2034 | 137 Every person who is guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is provided is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $100 and not more than $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than six months, or to both.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 137 (src:2034)
`s 137 the greatest fine` MEANS 2000

-- src:2034 | 137 Every person who is guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is provided is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $100 and not more than $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than six months, or to both.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 137 (src:2034)
`s 137 the longest term of imprisonment, in months` MEANS 6

-- src:2034 | 137 Every person who is guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is provided is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $100 and not more than $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than six months, or to both.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 137 (src:2034)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a penalty is provided for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 137 the person is liable on summary conviction to the general penalty` IF
        `the person is guilty of an offence under this Act`
    AND NOT (`a penalty is provided for the offence`)

-- "a fine of not less than $100 and not more than $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than six months, or to both":
-- a fine, or imprisonment, or both; each one imposed must be within its limits.
-- src:2034 | 137 Every person who is guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is provided is liable on summary conviction to a fine of not less than $100 and not more than $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than six months, or to both.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 137 (src:2034)
GIVEN `a fine is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine` IS A NUMBER
      `imprisonment is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 137 the punishment is within the limits` IF
        (`a fine is imposed` OR `imprisonment is imposed`)
    AND ((NOT (`a fine is imposed`)) OR (`the fine` AT LEAST `s 137 the least fine` AND `the fine` AT MOST `s 137 the greatest fine`))
    AND ((NOT (`imprisonment is imposed`)) OR `the term of imprisonment, in months` AT MOST `s 137 the longest term of imprisonment, in months`)

§ `Part VI -- Social Insurance Number`

§§ `s 138 Obligation`

-- "in respect of whom Part VII.1 applies" is outside this range (section 152.01, piece ei5), so it is an input.
-- src:2038 | 138 Every person employed in insurable employment, and every self-employed person in respect of whom Part VII.1 applies, must have a Social Insurance Number that has been assigned to that person under an Act of Parliament.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 138 (src:2038)
GIVEN `is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a self-employed person in respect of whom Part VII.1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 152.01 (piece ei5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 138 the person must have a Social Insurance Number assigned under an Act of Parliament` IF
       `is employed in insurable employment`
    OR `is a self-employed person in respect of whom Part VII.1 applies`

§§ `s 139 Change of name`

-- "unless they have already so informed another authority empowered to receive that information": in that case the duty does not arise.
-- src:2040 | 139 When the name of a person to whom a Social Insurance Number has been assigned changes because of marriage or otherwise, the person shall inform the Commission of their new name within 60 days after the day on which the change of name becomes effective, unless they have already so informed another authority empowered to receive that information.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 139 (src:2040)
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the person changes because of marriage or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has already informed another authority empowered to receive that information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 139 the person must inform the Commission of their new name` IF
        `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person`
    AND `the name of the person changes because of marriage or otherwise`
    AND NOT (`the person has already informed another authority empowered to receive that information`)

-- 60 days after the day on which the change of name becomes effective (F-ei4-1). NOTHING when the duty does not arise.
-- src:2040 | 139 When the name of a person to whom a Social Insurance Number has been assigned changes because of marriage or otherwise, the person shall inform the Commission of their new name within 60 days after the day on which the change of name becomes effective, unless they have already so informed another authority empowered to receive that information.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 139 (src:2040)
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the person changes because of marriage or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has already informed another authority empowered to receive that information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the change of name becomes effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 139 the last day on which the person must inform the Commission of their new name` IS
    IF `s 139 the person must inform the Commission of their new name`
            `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person`
            `the name of the person changes because of marriage or otherwise`
            `the person has already informed another authority empowered to receive that information`
    THEN JUST (`the last day of` 60 `days after` `the day on which the change of name becomes effective`)
    ELSE NOTHING

